        "text": "15"
      },
      {
        "y": 24.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 477.3,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Birth and death: from cradle to grave"
      },
      {
        "y": 67.8,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 190.3,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A At the beginning"
      },
      {
        "y": 90,
        "x0": 111.1,
        "x1": 477,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Pregnancy1 is the nine-month period when a woman is expecting a baby. It begins with"
      },
      {
        "y": 102,
        "x0": 111.1,
        "x1": 499.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "conception2, when the mother’s egg is fertilised3 and an embryo4 implants5 in the mother’s"
      },
      {
        "y": 114,
        "x0": 111.1,
        "x1": 511.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "womb, or uterus6. Most mothers conceive7 naturally but some are helped by fertility drugs8 or"
      },
      {
        "y": 126,
        "x0": 111.1,
        "x1": 506.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "other procedures such as IVF9. As the foetus10 grows, it is fed through the mother’s placenta11."
      },
      {
        "y": 138,
        "x0": 111.1,
        "x1": 510.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "After 40 weeks, the mother usually goes into labour12. If this doesn’t happen naturally, she may"
      },
      {
        "y": 150,
        "x0": 111.1,
        "x1": 507.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "be induced13. Usually, a mother is helped to give birth14 by a midwife15. Sometimes a surgeon"
      },
      {
        "y": 162,
        "x0": 111.1,
        "x1": 344.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "is needed to deliver16 the baby by caesarean section17."
      },
      {
        "y": 185.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 (adj. = pregnant) 2 time when sperm and egg meet and a baby starts to form 3 made to start developing"
      },
      {
        "y": 196.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "into new life 4 developing baby 5 fixes itself 6 organ inside the mother where the fertilised egg develops"
      },
      {
        "y": 208.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 498.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "into a baby; uterus is a more medical word than womb 7 become pregnant 8 drugs that help a woman"
      },
      {
        "y": 219.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 496.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to become pregnant 9 in vitro fertilisation: process that fertilises a woman’s egg in a laboratory; babies"
      },
      {
        "y": 231.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "born this way are sometimes referred to as test tube babies 10 what the embryo developing in the uterus"
      },
      {
        "y": 242.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 497,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "is known as from eight weeks onward 11 organ connecting the developing baby to the mother and giving it"
      },
      {
        "y": 254.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 507.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "food 12 goes into the last stage of pregnancy, where the womb starts the process of pushing the baby out of"
      },
      {
        "y": 265.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 300.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the body 13 be helped medically to start the process"
      },
      {
        "y": 274.1,
        "x0": 331.5,
        "x1": 425.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Language help"
      },
      {
        "y": 277.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 280.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of labour (noun = induction) 14 have her baby"
      },
      {
        "y": 288.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 280.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "15 person medically trained to help women when"
      },
      {
        "y": 298.4,
        "x0": 186.6,
        "x1": 505.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "16 Expect when it means ‘expect a baby’ is only"
      },
      {
        "y": 301.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 298.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "they are giving birth help the mother to give birth"
      },
      {
        "y": 310.4,
        "x0": 175.8,
        "x1": 507.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "17 used in the continuous form, e.g. Helena and"
      },
      {
        "y": 312.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 303,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(noun = delivery) operation in which the mother’s"
      },
      {
        "y": 321.9,
        "x0": 332.5,
        "x1": 498.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "her sister are both expecting (NOT expect)."
      },
      {
        "y": 324.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 302.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "abdomen and womb are cut open to allow the baby to"
      },
      {
        "y": 335.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 143.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "be removed"
      },
      {
        "y": 350.5,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 155.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B At the end"
      },
      {
        "y": 369.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 490.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "More and more people these days are living to a ripe old age1. My aunt, for example, that’s"
      },
      {
        "y": 381.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 490.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "my late2 father’s sister, is 93. She’s been a pensioner3 for more years than she worked. She"
      },
      {
        "y": 393.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 500.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "lives in sheltered accommodation4 but she’s not at all doddery5 or gaga6. She’s lucky still to"
      },
      {
        "y": 405.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 503.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "have all her wits about her7 because a lot of elderly people develop dementia8. Funerals are"
      },
      {
        "y": 417.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 500.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "changing a lot too. I went to one recently where there was a coffin9 in the colours of the dead"
      },
      {
        "y": 429.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 508.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "man’s football team. And at the wake,10 his sister told me she’d put it in her will11 that her own"
      },
      {
        "y": 441.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 508.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "ashes12 are to be sent up in a rocket! Funerals now are often more about celebrating a person’s"
      },
      {
        "y": 453.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 493.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "life rather than just about mourning13. As for me, I think I’d prefer an ordinary cremation14."
      },
      {
        "y": 465.8,
        "x0": 111.6,
        "x1": 424.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "But then I’d quite like to have my ashes scattered15 at sea, as I love sailing."
      },
      {
        "y": 483.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 living well into old age; usually used in the phrase to live to a ripe old age 2 now dead 3 elderly person,"
      },
      {
        "y": 494.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 493,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "receiving an old age pension from the state 4 special housing, usually for old people, where care staff also"
      },
      {
        "y": 505.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "live 5 weak and unable to walk well, usually because of old age; informal 6 unable to think clearly because"
      },
      {
        "y": 516.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of old age; informal and offensive 7 is still able to think and react quickly 8 an illness that causes problems"
      },
      {
        "y": 527.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 491.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "with memory loss 9 box where the dead person is put 10 gathering of family and friends after a funeral"
      },
      {
        "y": 539.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 496.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "11 legal document saying what is to happen to your possessions after your death 12 remains of a body after"
      },
      {
        "y": 550.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 472.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "cremation (see ) 13 expressing sadness after someone’s death (the mourners have been bereaved)"
      },
      {
        "y": 553.2,
        "x0": 155.5,
        "x1": 161.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "14"
      },
      {
        "y": 561.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "14 service at a place called a crematorium, where a dead body is burnt (as opposed to a burial, where the body"
      },
      {
        "y": 572.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 259.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "is buried in the ground) 15 spread around"
      },
      {
        "y": 588.3,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 248.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Death in different registers"
      },
      {
        "y": 606,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 521.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "expressions of sympathy: Please accept my condolences. (formal) I was so sorry to hear/learn of your"
      },
      {
        "y": 618,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 162,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "loss. (informal)"
      },
      {
        "y": 630,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 367.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "euphemisms for ‘to die’: to pass away, to pass on, to pass over"
      },
      {
        "y": 642,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 506.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "very informal expressions for being close to death: to be at death’s door, to be on your last legs"
      },
      {
        "y": 654.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 350.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "(often used about machines, e.g. My laptop’s on its last legs)"
      },
      {
        "y": 666,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 460.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "newspaper words: fatalities [dead people], perished [died], slaughtered [violently killed]"
      },
      {
        "y": 678,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 483,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "legal words: the deceased [the dead person], to bequeath [to leave something in a will; noun = a"
      },
      {
        "y": 690,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "bequest], to inherit [to receive something from someone who has died; noun = an inheritance], to die"
      },
      {
        "y": 702,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 248.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "intestate [without having made a will]"
      }
    ],
